med, those requests are added to your account and Trips says &quot;We found earlier requests made with your email&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-stuck-on-a-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stuck on a page?</h2><p class="gd-p">If you spend a few minutes on a page without anything saving, see the same error three times, or go back and forth between the same two steps, a small box asks <b class="gd-ui">Need a hand with</b> the page. <b class="gd-ui">Open the guide section</b> opens this guide at the right chapter beside the page (a sheet from the bottom on a phone); <b class="gd-ui">Back to what I was doing</b> closes it and everything you typed is still there. <b class="gd-ui">Not now</b> quiets it on that page for a day. It never shows while you pay or sign.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows <b class="gd-ui">We&#39;ve updated our terms</b>: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press <b class="gd-ui">Accept</b> to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-your-name-and-password-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your name and password (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Profile. <b class="gd-ui">Save my display name</b> changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press <b class="gd-ui">Request a name change</b>, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). <b class="gd-ui">Change my password</b> sends you to the password page.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'home-and-your-vehicles', 'chapter', 'apply-and-get-your-car-listed', 'Home tells you what to do next. Each car has its own page with its status, terms, bookings, invoices and photos.

## Home at a glance

1. The menu: Home, Cars (your cars and their bookings), Money (statements, payouts and invoices), Documents and Account (profile, banking and notifications). Each of Cars, Money and Account is one page with a row of tabs on top. Home starts with the next thing to do, then one line with what you earned so far this month, how many cars are out, the next payout and any fees due.
2. At the top: each car with its photo and its status right now (On rent, Available or In service), this month''s rental charges against last month, the next payout and the days rented this month.
3. Your earnings: a column per month. Press a month, or the arrows, for its bookings, days rented, rental charges, fees billed and the payout on its statement. Choose a car to see it alone, or **Payouts** for the statement amounts. Beside it, Money (what is due now, your fees each month, the next billing date and the next payout date) and Coming up, your next bookings.
4. Your vehicles: each car with this month so far, its next booking and what it needs next. Got another car? Press **Add a vehicle**.

![](/guides/img/owner-01-home-desktop-9035b084.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1270; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 19.1 8.1, 2 72.9 30.7, 3 31.2 85.0")

> Tip: When something needs you (a signature, a payment or an upload), it is the first thing on Home.

## A car''s page

Open Cars, then a car.

1. The top shows the car''s photo, its plate, how it is enrolled and its status right now.
2. Terms: the Insurance Fee, the Revenue Share, your enrolment date and a link to the listing.
3. This car by month (choose a month with the arrows or its column), Coming up, and Bookings with every trip in your car. **Book it for myself** reserves it for you.
4. Leaving explains the exit notice and has the button to give it.

![](/guides/img/owner-03-vehicle-desktop-7f1a9a38.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1242; address: carmacars.ca/owner/vehicles/1f21c3e5-39c3-4d54-ae0d-cbb2512835e7; pins: 1 55.6 25.1, 2 83.3 38.0, 3 36.5 54.5, 4 81.2 67.0")

While a car is being set up, its page also shows the onboarding checklist and the uploads it still needs: the ownership permit, the lender''s permission and the insurance.

## Service and maintenance

On a car''s page, under Service and maintenance.

- What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.
- Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.
- You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.
- It is read only: call or message us about a service.

## Take new listing photos

Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.

1. On the car''s page, press **Add listing photos** (or **Take new photos** for a car already live).
2. Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot in the list. Press **Retake** if one is not right.
4. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
5. Press **Submit for listing**. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg "phone; size: 390 610; pins: 4 92.3 43.4, 3 76.9 70.2")

## Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** shows the car''s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, **Cars** > **Cars you referred** shows their cars'' bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.', 'Home and your vehicles', 'What Home shows, each car''s page, adding a car and new listing photos.',
  'Home tells you what to do next. Each car has its own page with its status, terms, bookings, invoices and photos.

## Home at a glance

1. The menu: Home, Cars (your cars and their bookings), Money (statements, payouts and invoices), Documents and Account (profile, banking and notifications). Each of Cars, Money and Account is one page with a row of tabs on top. Home starts with the next thing to do, then one line with what you earned so far this month, how many cars are out, the next payout and any fees due.
2. At the top: each car with its photo and its status right now (On rent, Available or In service), this month''s rental charges against last month, the next payout and the days rented this month.
3. Your earnings: a column per month. Press a month, or the arrows, for its bookings, days rented, rental charges, fees billed and the payout on its statement. Choose a car to see it alone, or **Payouts** for the statement amounts. Beside it, Money (what is due now, your fees each month, the next billing date and the next payout date) and Coming up, your next bookings.
4. Your vehicles: each car with this month so far, its next booking and what it needs next. Got another car? Press **Add a vehicle**.

![](/guides/img/owner-01-home-desktop-9035b084.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1270; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 19.1 8.1, 2 72.9 30.7, 3 31.2 85.0")

> Tip: When something needs you (a signature, a payment or an upload), it is the first thing on Home.

## A car''s page

Open Cars, then a car.

1. The top shows the car''s photo, its plate, how it is enrolled and its status right now.
2. Terms: the Insurance Fee, the Revenue Share, your enrolment date and a link to the listing.
3. This car by month (choose a month with the arrows or its column), Coming up, and Bookings with every trip in your car. **Book it for myself** reserves it for you.
4. Leaving explains the exit notice and has the button to give it.

![](/guides/img/owner-03-vehicle-desktop-7f1a9a38.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1242; address: carmacars.ca/owner/vehicles/1f21c3e5-39c3-4d54-ae0d-cbb2512835e7; pins: 1 55.6 25.1, 2 83.3 38.0, 3 36.5 54.5, 4 81.2 67.0")

While a car is being set up, its page also shows the **Onboarding** checklist and the uploads it still needs: the ownership permit, the lender''s permission and the insurance.

## The onboarding checklist

Home and each car''s page show the same **Onboarding checklist**. Each step says one of four things: done, to do (and who it waits on: you, CarmaCars, or another office such as the registry), blocked (and why, for example "First: terms approved"), or not needed. A step that waits on you has one button: the one thing to do for it, such as **Check and sign** or **Upload the ownership permit**.

## Change an onboarding photo

A wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender''s letter? Open the car, then **Your onboarding photos**.

1. Press **Replace** and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.
2. Or press **Remove**, then **Remove the photo**.

> Good to know: Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.

## Add several cars at once

Open **Cars**, then **Add cars from a VIN list**.

1. Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.
2. Press **Preview**: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.
3. Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press **Add**.

Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.

## Service and maintenance

On a car''s page, under Service and maintenance.

- What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.
- Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.
- You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.
- It is read only: call or message us about a service.

## Take new listing photos

Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.

1. On the car''s page, press **Add listing photos** (or **Take new photos** for a car already live).
2. Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot in the list. Press **Retake** if one is not right.
4. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
5. Press **Submit for listing**. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg "phone; size: 390 610; pins: 4 92.3 43.4, 3 76.9 70.2")

## Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** shows the car''s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, **Cars** > **Cars you referred** shows their cars'' bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.',
