it opens to you when their claim runs out, or ask an Admin to take it over. Sales: a request from the website shows &quot;Opens to you at&quot; a time for its first 15 minutes, and a To do task says when it opens; after that whoever opens it first answers it, customer service included.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-an-enquiry-on-an-example-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An enquiry on an example car</h2><p class="gd-p">Some cars on the site are marked &quot;Example car&quot;: samples that show the kind of cars we rent. A request on one is an enquiry, never a booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The task Suggest a similar real car comes to To do with the enquiry number (EQ-1001 and up), the car asked for, the dates and the contact. When a real car was free for those dates, the task names it after <b class="gd-ui">Free:</b> (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price), and the person was told we have a similar car and will confirm it within 2 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the named car is still right for them (or find a real car of the same kind and price that is free for those dates), and make a <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> for it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Call or email the person with the car and the price, then mark the task done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Reply within the first reply target, as for any request. Never offer the example car itself: it does not exist.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-request-from-a-vehicle-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A request from a vehicle page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every make, model, year and trim page (carmacars.ca/cars/toyota/rav4/2023/xle, for example) has Request 