 say what we can find. We do not lend or lease: on a financing question, say so and offer the rental. For detailing or body shop work, give a time and a price, and always offer a rental while their car is in (an insurance replacement rental when it is a claim). For mechanical work (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task: an oil change, brakes, tires, a tow and the like), CarmaCars does not do the work: book it with a trusted shop or recommend one, never promise the shop&#39;s price or time, and offer a rental while their car is in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> as you go: contacted, qualified, converted or closed with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>We mostly rent cars. Never say a car is for sale unless an Admin flagged it; the page shows it with its price when one is.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-send-an-offer-to-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer to a caller</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> beside a car in Find a car). No request needed: one screen, and the renter has the link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Find the customer by name, phone or email, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a new customer</b>: full legal name, mobile, email and date of birth. Already on file with that email or phone? Use them: never a second record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car (by car code, plate or name; each says Free or Not free), the dates and the places.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The price: the rate sheet, a total or a rate per day, with the reason for a price you type. The deposit, discounts and fees are set by an Admin; customer service sets the Protection Plan price. Amounts I type, at the top of the price: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter pays, worked back to before tax for you. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out from it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">How the rental and the deposit are paid (card online, e-Transfer, cash, platform payout, the insurer; deposit by card hold, cash or e-Transfer), who found this client, the message, how long it is open (48 hours at most) and Email, Text or both.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Check the offer as the renter will see it on the right, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An offer that is out is changed in place: <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, change it, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and send the update</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Save without telling the renter</b>. No need to withdraw it first.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-new-quote-for-a-caller" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New quote for a caller</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b>. Choose the Car, the Pickup and Return (at least 2 hours from now).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the lead came in, then the caller&#39;s Full legal name, Email, Mobile and Date of birth.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set the Licence class and Damage cover, and note places, extras and what they asked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Create the request</b>. It opens like any request; send the offer from there.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/quotes/new</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1220/1260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-05-new-quote-desktop-4e386b1c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1220" height="1260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:15.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:41.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.1%;top:72.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:63.9%;top:85.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-edit-a-booking-a-fee-or-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking, a fee or the renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking that is confirmed, on trip or returned is edited directly; the renter&#39;s details are corrected from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>: the return (extend or shorten), the car, the rental charge, each fee, the kilometres and the note. Tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Money tab, Fees, <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>: a fee forgotten (the young driver fee shows its price for the dates) or a charge of its own.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, or record cash or an e-Transfer (Rental charges, Collect (the amount) rental, <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>: a wrong email, phone, name, licence or address. A new email is their sign-in at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same renter twice? Under the renter, Possible duplicates: <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves everything of the other record here.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is recorded with your name, the time, the reason and the before and after.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-renter-messages-and-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter messages and Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter messages</b> lists the latest messages with their booking. Open the booking to reply, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Find a renter</b>: search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To open a renter&#39;s private details, press <b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>. The reason is kept in the access log.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/messages</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/260"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-06-messages-desktop-3441fa91.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="260"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:48.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> (fleet: under Cars). You enter everything for the owner; they never fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line with the year, make, model, trim and details (Edit if something is wrong). No VIN at hand: add it by its plate and choose the year, make and model. Tap the colour and check the class. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them. Photos are optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: what was agreed with the owner, to the cent. An Admin checks them before anything is sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner. The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and send to an Admin</b>. The application waits in the Admin&#39;s Applications, marked Entered by staff with your name. When the Admin approves, the owner gets one email to review and sign.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A fleet supplier (a corporation leasing its cars to CarmaCars): choose New owner, <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then Route <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>. The default lease terms are set at once. For the car, enter the VIN, the plate and the ownership copy, choose its tier, <b class="gd-ui">Regular</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Troubled</b> (it is set once), and who it is registered to now (for a car moving in or bought, the name and address on the ownership and the date). Its ServiceOntario forms are filled in at once. No terms, no invoices and no paper signing: the supplier signs in the owner portal. The car goes on the lease when an Admin approves it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owners-the-checklist-the-photos-and-the-forms-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners: the checklist, the photos and the forms (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> (customer service and fleet), then an owner. Search finds any owner by name, email, plate or VIN.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>: per car, each step done, to do (and who it waits on), blocked (and why) or not needed, with the one button to press.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding photos</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> (with a reason) a wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender&#39;s letter, or <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or mark it <b class="gd-ui">Not accepted</b> (the owner reads why). A replaced photo is checked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>: each ServiceOntario form the car needs, made by themselves, with its status, the date it was made and its download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a list of VINs</b> for the owner: paste or upload, <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-owner-forms-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner forms (Forms C and D)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Each row is a scan an owner uploaded before November 2026 (Forms C and D are signed on screen since then), with the witnesses and the status.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the scan. Check every page is there and signed, with each witness&#39;s signature and name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/300"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-08-owner-forms-desktop-eceaee0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="300"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.6%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:36.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-rental-agreements-are-signed-online-only" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental agreements are signed online only</h2><p class="gd-p">A rental agreement, or a booking change, is signed by the renter in their portal or on the phone at the handover (the e-signature). A copy signed on paper is not accepted or recorded: send the renter the link again from the booking. One recorded before November 2026 stays readable under Signed on paper.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter or an additional driver who has not signed yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. Confirm the name and that you saw the original licence, then <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> the signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>: they sign on their own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The licence comes first: the renter uploads it from the request, and the offer cannot be accepted without it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-the-booking-s-rental-agreements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The booking&#39;s rental agreements</h2><p class="gd-p">The Rental agreements card keeps both agreements in step with the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Any change after signing makes a new version by itself. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage waits for the renter&#39;s signature: they get the link by email and text, and the card says &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fields still blank (a licence expiry, an insurer&#39;s policy number) are listed: type them and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>. Check-in stops on a field a claim needs until it is filled or an Admin overrides.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every signature: a code to the signer&#39;s phone or email, the key terms initialled, three consents, a drawn signature.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-check-renter-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check renter documents</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage, before the handover.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task &quot;identity documents or coverage proof to review&quot;, or open the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Review</b> shows the documents of any booking being arranged or under way, with no task needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every licence image, selfie and proof of coverage of the booking is on one screen, with what to check written once above them: the selfie matches, no alteration, the coverage is active to the return date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under each driver, the licence reader lists what it read (from the back&#39;s barcode, else the photo) and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos sharp and whole, valid to the return, class accepted, old enough at pickup, name and date of birth match the driver, the Ontario number, front and back the same licence, and the main driver&#39;s Ontario licence. Look closely at each Flag.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: everything still waiting is approved at once (the Protection Plan too). A document the system refuses is named with the reason; the rest are approved.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening is logged. An Admin can do the same from Admin &gt; To do. Field staff review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from their My jobs: the booking history says the role, field.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Main driver: Ontario licence needed. When the main driver&#39;s licence is from elsewhere, they are moved to additional driver (their photos and checks stay; you still review them) and pickup is blocked until a driver with an Ontario licence is the main driver. The renter adds one from their booking. Only an Admin can undo the swap or let it go with a reason.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Which credit cards include rental car coverage?</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters ask this often. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> (every function has it under Rentals or Bookings) is your quick reference: what to say, what to check, and the list.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Send the renter <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span>: each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), longest rental, key exclusions, its official guide and the day we last checked it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Ask which car they want. Most Canadian cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and many luxury models are priced higher. Give them the car&#39;s model year and trim so they can check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Never tell a renter they are covered. Their card&#39;s issuer decides that: ask them to call the number on the back of their card about this car and these dates. CarmaCars does not decide claims.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Over the limit, an excluded make, a debit card or a longer rental than the card allows: offer OPCF 27 on their own auto policy or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card marked Unverified came from a published summary, not the issuer&#39;s guide. Something wrong or out of date in the list? Tell an Admin: they correct it in Settings &gt; Card coverage.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters are asked for a review by email and text after each trip. <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Review requests</b> shows the ones on hold and the Google reviews to match.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: the booking has a charge that is not settled or waived yet (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls) or an open incident. It leaves the list by itself once the charges are settled or waived.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The renter should be asked now anyway? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b>. Should never be asked? Press <b class="gd-ui">Do not ask</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google reviews: a possible match to a renter shows &quot;possible match&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> if it is them, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> if not, or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b> with the booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking, the card Review requests has <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> (for example after a call that went well) and <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> when the renter says they already left one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Never offer anything for a review and never ask only happy renters: everyone gets the same message and the same Google link.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s Changes tab you can propose new dates, times or another car, as an Admin does: set the change, write the reason, press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>. The renter has 48 hours to accept and sign the amendment. You also send a new signing link to an additional driver from the booking screen.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-a-late-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking past its return time shows the late return panel. The renter can still extend in their booking while they have the car: the extension counts from the original return time, it is approved at once when the car is free, and paying it stops the late notices. Point them to <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b> first. Otherwise work it in order:</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Button</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Log a call</b></td><td>Record each call to the renter and what they said.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T13</b></td><td>The first late notice email.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Send T14 (final notice)</b></td><td>The final notice.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Request disable</b></td><td>Ask an Admin to approve disabling the car.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Open an incident</b></td><td>When the car is not coming back as planned.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-booked-when-the-renter-accepts-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booked when the renter accepts (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter who approves the offer has booked the car, even before paying: the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> and holds the car everywhere. Collect the payment before the pickup (a <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> To do comes 48 hours before). When you send an offer, the renter&#39;s view is right under <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="customer-service-book-it-now-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book it now (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, tick <b class="gd-ui">Book it now (no renter approval)</b> when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, then take the card on this device. Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: &quot;Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone&quot;. It shows a card; <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'fleet', 'chapter', 'finance', 'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, given to the field staff member with the fewest jobs that day. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **Assign**, **Reassign**, **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Only Admins and fleet staff see positions.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plate box is suggested by itself on every outside photo as the listing opens (Box suggested). Press **Cover the plate** and check it; **Suggest the plate** asks again. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**, then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; the late charges follow it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.
